cff-version: "1.2.0"
title: "CiMind: Deterministic Epistemic Memory, Sub-5ms Ambient Safety Reflexes, and Longitudinal Drift Guards for Local-First Cognitive Care Research"
message: "If you use CiMind or reference its safety and epistemic memory invariants in research or hardware evaluations, please cite this software using the metadata below."
type: software
version: "0.2.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24504136"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/TinkeringDao/CiMind"
url: "https://tinkeringdao.dev/research/cimind/"
abstract: >-
  Local-first, zero-cloud, cryptographically auditable Python reference kernel
  for aging-in-place and mild-to-advanced cognitive impairment (GDS 1-7)
  smart-home research. Places deterministic verification seams—a four-zone
  epistemic memory firewall, sub-5ms camera-free sensor-fusion safety and
  LoRaWAN perimeter reflexes, stage- and mother-tongue-adaptive dialogue
  constraints, and 21-day intra-patient Median/MAD longitudinal and
  pharmacovigilance sentinels—around untrusted local language models and
  multi-modal residential sensors.
